# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[Christian]] [[house of worship]]; a building where Christian [[religious]] [[service]]s take place. {{defdate|from 9th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|There is a lovely little '''church''' in the valley.}}
#: {{ux|en|This building used to be a '''church''' before being converted into a library.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Bucky and Friends|page=117|author=John R. Dodd|year=2007|passage=He got the message and was in '''church''' the next Sunday. We need to stay in church with the fellowship of others in order to keep the fire of faith burning brightly.}}
# [[Christian]]s collectively seen as a single spiritual [[community]]; [[Christianity]]; [[Christendom]]. {{defdate|from 9th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|These worshippers make up the '''Church''' of Christ.}}
#* [[Acts]] 20:28, New International Version:
#*: Be shepherds of the '''church''' of God, which he bought with his own blood.
# {{lb|en|countable}} A local group of people who follow the same Christian religious beliefs, local or general. {{defdate|from 9th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Ultimate Church Sound Operator's Handbook|page=78|author=Bill Gibson|year=2007|passage=Many young people find their only role models of family life in '''church'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Bucky and Friends|page=117|author=John R. Dodd|year=2007|passage=He got the message and was in church the next Sunday. We need to stay in '''church''' with the fellowship of others in order to keep the fire of faith burning brightly.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Enhancing understanding the church through preaching on ...|page=61|author=Yil Gyoung Kang|year=2008|passage=As they actively get involved in ministry, lay ministry becomes vigorous, and new believers will settle in '''church''' with more ease.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Souls in Transition|page=194|author=Christian Smith|coauthors=Patricia Snell|year=2009|passage=she had very many adults in '''church''' with whom she could talk about issues in life.}}
#*{{quote-book|en|url=https://books.google.com.tr/books?id=XIMrAAAAYAAJ&q=%22+++become+a+saint%22%22subject:%22fiction%22&dq=%22+++become+a+saint%22%22subject:%22fiction%22|title=Right as Rain|author=Bev Marshall|publisher=Ballantine Books|isbn=9780345468413|lccn=2003063775|oclc=1037233008|year=2004|page=130|passage=Ruthie had left the '''church''' disappointed , reluctant to give up the idea that she was chosen by God to become a saint . But within a month she had sinned by lying , masturbating , and coveting Sarah 130 • Beu Marshall.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A particular [[denomination]] of [[Christianity]]. {{defdate|from 9th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''Church''' of England separated from the Roman Catholic '''Church''' in 1534.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|countable|as bare noun}} Christian [[worship]] held at a church; [[service]]. {{defdate|from 10th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Redeeming the South: Religious Cultures and Racial Identities ...|page=119|author=Paul Harvey|year=1997|passage=Pastors complained that they were not allowed enough authority in '''church''', with women exercising too much informal control.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Disturbing Questions...: Solid Answers|page=174|author=Lee Roberson|year=2000|passage=Some people are always saying, "Oh, you have too much '''church'''." You never get too much '''church'''. I go to '''church''' every day.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=On a Journey with God: You Come Too|page=53|author=George Shillington|year=2003|passage=the learned women will be qualified to lead '''in church''' with equal grace and equal insight and equal gifts.}}
# {{label|en|uncountable}} [[organized religion|Organized religion]] in general or a specific [[religion]] considered as a [[political]] [[institution]].
#: {{usex|en|Many constitutions enshrine the separation of '''church''' and state.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1903|author=w:Duncan Black MacDonald|title=Development of Muslim Theology, Jurisprudence and Constitutional Theory|page=4|text=But in Muslim countries, '''Church''' and State are one indissolubly, and until the very essence of Islam passes away, that unity cannot be relaxed. The law of the land, too, is, in theory, the law of the '''Church'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1991|author=Cyril E. Black; et al.|title=The Modernization of Inner Asia|url=https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=FoIE4laY7JcC&lpg=PP1&pg=PA15#v=onepage&q=%22Because%20the%20pan-Buddhist%20movement%20was%20heavily%20supported%20by%20the%20Japanese%22&f=false|page=15|text=Because the pan-Buddhist movement was heavily supported by the Japanese in Inner Mongolia, the Buddhist '''church''', already under attack by Soviet-backed antireligion campaigns in Outer Mongolia, was further damaged {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Ayelet Shachar|title=Multicultural Jurisdictions: Cultural Differences and Women's Rights|page=72|url=https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=E87C6qTgHscC&lpg=PA72&pg=PA72#v=onepage&q=%22The%20secular%20absolutist%20model%20is%20based%20on%20a%20strict%20separation%20between%22&f=false|text=The secular absolutist model is based on a strict separation between '''church''' and state.}}
